WHO   — The Popek-Goldberg Theorem (1974) — The doctrinal test: an architecture is efficiently virtualizable IFF its sensitive instructions are a subset of its privileged ones — every state-exposing instruction must TRAP to the supervisor. The rule every CPU was measured against for 30 years.
